# .spool/lookup/lookup.req

feature: LOOKUP

requirements:

  - id: LOOKUP-1
    title: Requirement Lookup by ID
    description: >
      The get_requirement tool must return a single requirement
      identified by its Spool ID, including its acceptance
      criteria and the tests linked to each AC.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-05-06
    rationale: >
      Looking up a single requirement is the agent's primary
      entry point when it is about to write or modify code that
      should satisfy a known ID. Returning the full requirement
      with its ACs and linked tests in one call lets the agent
      see the requirement, its acceptance bar, and the existing
      test surface without follow-up calls.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: LOOKUP-1-1
        title: Known Requirement Returned
        description: >
          Given a Spool ID matching a requirement in the
          project,
          when get_requirement is invoked,
          then the result includes the requirement's id, title,
          description, status, feature, source file, and its
          acceptance criteria, with each AC carrying its
          linked tests as function name, file, and line.

      - id: LOOKUP-1-2
        title: Unknown ID Returns Null
        description: >
          Given a syntactically valid Spool ID that does not
          match any requirement in the project,
          when get_requirement is invoked,
          then the result is null and no error is returned.

      - id: LOOKUP-1-3
        title: AC ID Returns Null
        description: >
          Given an ID that matches an acceptance criterion but
          not a requirement,
          when get_requirement is invoked,
          then the result is null and no error is returned.

  - id: LOOKUP-2
    title: Acceptance Criterion Lookup by ID
    description: >
      The get_acceptance_criterion tool must return a single
      AC identified by its Spool ID, including a summary of
      its parent requirement and any tests linked to it.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-05-06
    rationale: >
      Acceptance criteria are the units of behavior tests
      annotate, so an agent writing or reviewing a test will
      most often start from an AC ID rather than a requirement
      ID. Including the parent requirement summary in the
      response lets the agent understand the AC's context
      without a second call.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: LOOKUP-2-1
        title: Known AC Returned
        description: >
          Given a Spool ID matching an acceptance criterion in
          the project,
          when get_acceptance_criterion is invoked,
          then the result includes the AC's id, title,
          description, parent requirement id, parent requirement
          title, feature, source file, and its linked tests as
          function name, file, and line.

      - id: LOOKUP-2-2
        title: Unknown ID Returns Null
        description: >
          Given a syntactically valid Spool ID that does not
          match any acceptance criterion in the project,
          when get_acceptance_criterion is invoked,
          then the result is null and no error is returned.

      - id: LOOKUP-2-3
        title: Requirement ID Returns Null
        description: >
          Given an ID that matches a requirement but not an
          acceptance criterion,
          when get_acceptance_criterion is invoked,
          then the result is null and no error is returned.

  - id: LOOKUP-3
    title: Requirement Listing
    description: >
      The list_requirements tool must return summaries of every
      requirement in the project, optionally narrowed by feature
      and status, without inlining acceptance criteria.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-05-06
    rationale: >
      A listing tool is the agent's discovery mechanism — it is
      how a fresh agent learns what exists in the project. The
      filters mirror the two dimensions agents most often want
      to slice on. Acceptance criteria are deliberately omitted
      from the listing because including them turns this into
      an unbounded payload on any non-trivial project; agents
      that need ACs should follow up with get_requirement on
      specific IDs.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: LOOKUP-3-1
        title: All Requirements Listed
        description: >
          Given a tool call with no filters,
          when list_requirements is invoked,
          then the result contains an entry for every
          requirement in the project, each with id, title,
          status, feature, and source file.

      - id: LOOKUP-3-2
        title: Feature Filter Narrows
        description: >
          Given a tool call with a feature argument,
          when list_requirements is invoked,
          then the result is limited to requirements whose
          feature matches the argument.

      - id: LOOKUP-3-3
        title: Status Filter Narrows
        description: >
          Given a tool call with a status argument,
          when list_requirements is invoked,
          then the result is limited to requirements whose
          status matches the argument.

      - id: LOOKUP-3-4
        title: ACs Not Inlined
        description: >
          Given any tool call,
          when list_requirements is invoked,
          then no acceptance criteria are inlined in the
          returned entries.

      - id: LOOKUP-3-5
        title: Stable Ordering
        description: >
          Given any tool call,
          when list_requirements is invoked,
          then the result is sorted by requirement id so that
          repeated calls against the same project state return
          entries in the same order.

  - id: LOOKUP-4
    title: Feature Listing
    description: >
      The list_features tool must return every feature defined
      in the project together with the number of requirements
      and acceptance criteria it contains.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-05-06
    rationale: >
      Features are the top-level grouping in Spool's hierarchy
      and are the natural entry point for an agent that wants to
      orient itself before drilling into specific requirements.
      Including counts on each feature lets the agent gauge
      scope without a follow-up call.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: LOOKUP-4-1
        title: All Features Listed
        description: >
          Given a project with one or more features,
          when list_features is invoked,
          then the result contains an entry for every feature
          with its name, requirement count, and acceptance
          criterion count.

      - id: LOOKUP-4-2
        title: Stable Ordering
        description: >
          Given a tool call,
          when list_features is invoked,
          then the result is sorted alphabetically by feature
          name.

      - id: LOOKUP-4-3
        title: Empty Project Returns Empty List
        description: >
          Given a project with no .req files,
          when list_features is invoked,
          then the result is an empty list and no error.
